Reject `thresholds` values at configuration load that the check misread, crashed on, ignored, or would breach for every process count (numeric strings such as `'5'` or `'inf'`, booleans, NaN, a positive infinite lower bound, a negative infinite upper bound, a lower bound above the upper bound, or an infinite value past the two bounds), so an instance with such a value now fails to load and sends no metrics instead of running.
